The panic locks similar, but it is different.
We even have a different panic vector 0x660 instead of 0x670.
That really means that the EISA slot number did something good.
What we see is a oanic that happens when probing the secondary PCI
bus - we are over the EISA stuff at this point.
The brigde seems to be onboard and according to SRM you have 3 chips
behind it.
I don't know how good we are with PCI-bridges on AS2100A.
Please try to remove all PCI cards from that bus and see if it makes
a difference.
If it boots then try shuffling the cards.

